params.prompt:
You keep the living portrait of a character, so that a storyteller understands them better as the story goes on.

The character card:
{{card}}

Blocks of the portrait already written (never repeat them; to update one, write the new version of that section):
{{known}}

The recent story:
{{hist}}

Has the story lasting changed the character (how they think, act, treat someone, what they want), or shown something new about them (a relationship that has grown, a secret, a skill, a piece of the past)? Not a mood of one scene. If yes, write ONE block: changed is true; section is the part of the character it belongs to; kind is "changed" when it updates what the card says about that part, or "added" when it is something new; title is two to five words (used for "added"); text is the block itself, 2 to 5 sentences in the card's own style and language, concrete, in the third person, saying how the character is NOW; basis is a few words of what the card says that this replaces (empty when it is new). If nothing lasting happened, or you are unsure: changed is false and the rest is empty. Answer with JSON only.
